column2:
All beings everywhere and always reap what they themselves have done; here no one does anything, good or ill, to anyone else.
brahmapuran:136:20	As is the seed that is sown, so is the fruit; a mango never grows anywhere from the seed of a neem.
brahmapuran:136:21	Those who have not served the Gautami, have not worshipped Hari and Shankara, and have not given to brahmins — how can they be vessels of fortune?
brahmapuran:136:22	You have given nothing to brahmins, nor to me. Only what is given here awaits one in the next world.
brahmapuran:136:23	Because you always perform rites of purity with earth, water, kusha grass and mantras, and have dried up your body with austerity, you are pure of soul;
brahmapuran:136:24	but without giving, men nowhere obtain enjoyments. By doing good works a man becomes pure, and then detached;
brahmapuran:136:25	then, with unobstructed knowledge, he becomes liberated while living. Liberation is easy for all through devotion to me here, in full;
brahmapuran:136:26	enjoyment comes through giving and the like, and through relieving the suffering of all beings. Otherwise you will gain liberation through devotion, but you will not gain enjoyment.
